doctype html
html(lang="en")
  head
    meta(charset="utf-8")
    meta(name="viewport", content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1")
    title Behind the name — Longstream Distillery
    meta(name="description", content="How Longstream's Blonde Gin got its name, and the story behind the woman on the label.")
    //- Dark logo by default (shows on light tab bars); white logo in dark mode
    link(rel="icon", type="image/png", href="/images/logo.png")
    link(rel="icon", type="image/png", href="/images/logo-white.png", media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)")
    link(rel="preconnect", href="https://fonts.googleapis.com")
    link(rel="preconnect", href="https://fonts.gstatic.com", crossorigin="crossorigin")
    link(href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400;1,500&family=Jost:wght@300;400;500&display=swap", rel="stylesheet")
    link(rel="stylesheet", href="/styles/v5.css")
    link(rel="stylesheet", href="/styles/blonde.css")

  body
    include _nav

    main
      //- MASTHEAD — the label image sits behind the title, heavily faded, so the
      //- page opens on the very face it goes on to explain.
      section.bl-head
        .bl-head-art
          img(src="/images/blonde-girl/label.webp", onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='/images/blonde-girl/label.jpg'", alt="", aria-hidden="true")
        .wrap
          .v5-rule.center
          p.v5-kicker Behind the label
          h1.bl-title
            | Behind the name Blonde Gin
            span.bl-title-line and the image on the bottles
          p.bl-lead Every bottle label has a story, but ours started with a sunset and a bit of overconfidence.

      //- THE DARE
      section.bl-chapter
        .wrap
          .bl-prose
            p.bl-drop While sitting on our deck at Flatpoint, South Wairarapa, my wife Nikke and I were enjoying a bottle of gin. I foolishly — or maybe bravely — boasted that I could make a gin just as good as the commercial giant we were sipping.
            p.bl-beat The challenge was on.

      //- THE NAME
      section.bl-chapter.bl-chapter-alt
        .wrap
          .bl-prose
            p.v5-kicker The name
            p From the day we met, my nickname for Nikke was #[span.bl-nickname “Blondie”]. So Blonde Gin made sense as the name on the label.

      //- THE IMAGE
      section.bl-chapter
        .wrap
          .bl-prose
            p.v5-kicker The image
            p When it came to designing the imagery on the label, I paired an early image of Nikke with another image that stuck with me… A blonde woman in an advert, smiling with her eyes closed, utterly consumed by a moment of bliss.
            p I imagined her taking that first, perfect sip of gin and being overtaken by pure, unfettered joy.

          //- Two sources, one result. The + and = carry the whole idea, so they
          //- stay in place on mobile too, between the stacked cards.
          .bl-fusion
            figure.bl-fig
              .bl-fig-frame
                img(src="/images/blonde-girl/nikke.webp", onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='/images/blonde-girl/nikke.jpg'", alt="An early image of Nikke", width="363", height="324", loading="lazy")
              figcaption
                span.bl-fig-cap An early image of Nikke
            .bl-op(aria-hidden="true") +
            figure.bl-fig
              .bl-fig-frame
                img(src="/images/blonde-girl/inspiration.webp", onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='/images/blonde-girl/inspiration.jpg'", alt="The blonde woman from the advert, smiling with her eyes closed", width="368", height="294", loading="lazy")
              figcaption
                span.bl-fig-cap The woman in the advert
            .bl-op(aria-hidden="true") =
            figure.bl-fig.bl-fig-final
              .bl-fig-frame
                img(src="/images/blonde-girl/label.webp", onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='/images/blonde-girl/label.jpg'", alt="The fused portrait used on every Blonde bottle label", width="368", height="343", loading="lazy")
              figcaption
                span.bl-fig-cap The image on every Blonde bottle

          .bl-prose
            p.bl-close The final image is a creative fusion of both. It isn’t a direct portrait, but a heartfelt homage to Nikke, a kept promise, and the feeling of pure happiness.

      //- WHERE TO NEXT
      section.bl-outro
        .wrap
          p.bl-outro-sign Ross Remnant, Founder &amp; Distiller
          .bl-actions
            a.v5-btn-solid(href="/#range") See the Blonde range
            a.v5-btn-ghost(href="/") Back to home

    include _footer

    include _navscroll
    include _agegate
